WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.467
You're a fantastic guest. I love when you're on the show.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.701
I really am a fan.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:06.801
Every time you come on, we do something silly

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:09.634
or we get in some game or talk or do something.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.267
But the last time you were on,

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.300
we did the Musical Genre Challenge.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.467
-Ah, yes. -And we actually --

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:16.834
It inspired a song

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:20.300
that you wrote and became a giant hit.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.834
-If you don't know, I sang like this --

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:25.434
♪ We don't talk anymore ♪ And you guys played with me.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:27.434
-Yeah, you were doing Michael McDonald.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:29.634
♪ We don't talk anymore ♪

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.868
-♪ Like we used to do ♪

00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:33.667
♪ He had a place in... ♪

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.968
Michael McDonald just yawns when he sings.

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:39.100
And I was working with Calvin Harris

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.634
a couple of months ago.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:44.534
And he wanted to write a song with me,

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.300
and I sang it with my normal voice

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.067
that you hear on the radio and whatnot.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.367
And it just didn't feel as good,

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.968
so I just sang it in the Michael McDonald impression,

00:00:53.968 --> 00:00:57.334
and the dude's like -- It's the first single on the album.

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:59.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:01.901
-I loved it. I love hearing that story.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.100
It really made me happy, and I'm so happy

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.033
if I had anything to do inspire you

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:10.133
for the next hit -- generations to come.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:12.901
You worked with a bunch of famous people that we love,

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.000
and I just figured I'd run down a couple stories quickly

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.200
just to see if you remember any of these stories.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.067
Adam Sandler was here a few months ago

00:01:19.067 --> 00:01:20.434
and told us that you and Halsey

00:01:20.434 --> 00:01:23.300
performed for his daughter's sweet 16.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:25.200
-Yeah, and I don't do that too often,

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.067
but when Adam Sandler calls --

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.133
I drove myself. [ Laughter ]

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:31.400
-"I'm there, Adam." Yeah. -I live ten minutes away

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:33.167
from the country club that it was at,

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:35.601
and I never do that but for Adam Sandler.

00:01:35.601 --> 00:01:38.868
It's crazy to have Adam Sandler FaceTime you, by the way.

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:40.367
[ Laughter ] -Yeah.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.501
-Because he does it in his Billy Madison voice. "Charlie!"

00:01:42.501 --> 00:01:45.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.467 --> 00:01:47.133
Pink glasses on. He's such a cool guy.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:49.234
-He's the greatest guy, yeah.

00:01:49.234 --> 00:01:50.434
And he's just like...

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.434
[as Sandler] "Why don't you do this?"

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.200
[ Laughter ] -That's better.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.033
-"Come on." -That's better.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:59.267
-I'll do anything for Adam Sandler. Come on. Greatest.

00:01:59.267 --> 00:02:00.667
He said you crushed it.

00:02:00.667 --> 00:02:02.567
There's a story about running into Harry Styles

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.033
at a restaurant... -Oh, man.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:06.267
-...and you accidentally blowing up his spot.

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.100
-Yeah. It was 2014.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:11.133
I had just signed my first record contract.

00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:15.100
And I had never been to a fancy L.A. sushi restaurant.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:17.601
There's this place called Sushi Park in West Hollywood.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:20.267
And I was eating,

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:24.801
and then Jeff and Harry walked in --

00:02:24.801 --> 00:02:26.567
his manager, Jeff. -Oh, yeah.

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.934
-I didn't know him at the time, but I was just --

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:31.667
I don't get, like, smitten with anybody.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.000
At the time, I was just, like -- had whole-body chills.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.167
I was like, "I can't bel--" He he had a hat on.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.033 --> 00:02:40.033
-So you just go like, "Wow. Cool."

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:42.400
-It was very 2014 One Direction era.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.267
[ Laughter ] -Yeah.

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:47.634
-And I, for whatever reason, took out my phone

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.834
and I was like, "You're not gonna believe this.

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:51.334
What a week in L.A.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.701
I sign a record contract.

00:02:53.701 --> 00:02:55.701
And who walks in? None other than Harry Styles."

00:02:55.701 --> 00:02:59.501
And then 15 paparazzi are out front in like five minutes.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.667
-Everyone in the world knows that he's in that restaurant.

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:04.534
-He looks at me, and he just does a nod and follows me.

00:03:04.534 --> 00:03:06.367
I don't know if that was a good follow.

00:03:06.367 --> 00:03:08.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:09.634
And that's it.

00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:11.300
-Yeah, and you haven't heard from him since.

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.801
-No, haven't heard from him since.

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.567
I don't think he likes me very much.

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.734
-Yeah, he does. Yeah, he does. He's a nice guy.

00:03:17.734 --> 00:03:18.968
He loves you.

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:20.501
There's a --

00:03:20.501 --> 00:03:23.334
There's a scene in your video for "Light Switch,"

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:26.267
which, by the way, over 113 million views.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:27.601
Not too shabby, bud.

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:29.367
-Yeah, not that I was -- Not that we were checking.

00:03:29.367 --> 00:03:30.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:35.067
-But in the video, you're painting a red fence.

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:36.467
Now, I'm just saying,

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:39.801
a lot of Taylor Swift fans came out and said, "Ooh."

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:41.767
Maybe a possibility

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:44.801
you're hinting about something, an Easter egg.

00:03:44.801 --> 00:03:47.467
Charlie. Char-- [ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.501
Charlie. Charlie and Taylor?!

00:03:49.501 --> 00:03:51.100
No. What are you saying?

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:53.300
-No, I think we've spoken once.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:56.834
But that would be great.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:59.200
-Okay. Alright. Alright. That's good.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.367
So you can confirm that --

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:02.934
-We know each other one time.

00:04:02.934 --> 00:04:05.167
-Okay. Perfect. That's good.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.133
Congrats on the album.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.400
This is -- "Charlie" is the name of the album.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.434
-Thank you. -Yeah. It's a big hit.

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:15.300
A lot of people are calling this your ugly-cry album.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:17.234
[ Laughter ] -Yeah, sure.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:20.033
I mean, I was -- Maybe the reason why they say that

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.901
is because I was going through a lot of good things

00:04:22.901 --> 00:04:26.567
and bad things at the same time.

00:04:26.567 --> 00:04:28.067
-Nothing like a good ugly cry.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.901
-It was like a black-and-white cookie,

00:04:29.901 --> 00:04:31.868
which is probably why this is black-and-white.

00:04:31.868 --> 00:04:34.000
And me being the sound guy, I'm thinking,

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:38.133
"Well, what is the feeling happy and sad coming together

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:39.501
at the same time sound like?"

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:42.567
Well, I had 12 tracks in my mind,

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:45.767
and on one track you have really pretty roads.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:47.667
That represents the happy time in my life.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:50.367
And the really ugly bass like -- Pbhbhbhbhbht-pbbhthtt --

00:04:50.367 --> 00:04:52.767
playing at the same time as the happy roads.

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.467
And you do that 12 times, and you have a happy and sad --

00:04:55.467 --> 00:04:58.667
Because I made this -- I produced this record myself.

00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:01.334
Due to the pandemic, I couldn't be around a lot of songwriters.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:04.167
-I was following you on all the socials, on TikTok,

00:05:04.167 --> 00:05:07.567
and you were doing that -- I know, right?

00:05:07.567 --> 00:05:09.267
I'm not stalking you. I'm not stalking you.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:11.834
But you're a good follow. So I was --

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:13.968
But you were doing this thing for "Left and Right."

00:05:13.968 --> 00:05:16.167
You're like, "Hey, I think I might invent this song."

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:19.100
Where it is just -- comes out of the left speaker.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:23.300
-Right, right, because I was listening to "Yellow Submarine"

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.701
by the Beatles -- and "Lady Madonna."

00:05:26.701 --> 00:05:29.868
And if you don't know, due to the limitations of the recording

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.634
that they had at the time,

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.801
you had 8 tracks recording off an 8-track.

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.467
And sometimes Paul's voice would end up on the left side

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:37.801
of the speaker with a hi-hat.

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:41.067
And if you had a busted speaker system

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.701
and it was just monophonic,

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.868
you'd only hear the instrumental.

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:48.667
And I thought, well, why has no one ever taken advantage of that

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:51.067
and written a song that has lyrics like that,

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:54.067
where you're singing on the left-hand side of the speaker?

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.467
What if you're in your car

00:05:55.467 --> 00:05:57.834
and I'm on your left-hand side of your brain

00:05:57.834 --> 00:05:59.634
and then on you're right-hand side of your brain?

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.267
-No, seriously.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:03.300
But you walked us through this writing process,

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.133
and you made a giant song, by the way.

00:06:06.133 --> 00:06:10.167
-Yeah, well, I mean, my whole thing on TikTok

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.734
is to prove that anything,

00:06:11.734 --> 00:06:14.367
anything in this world can be made into music.

00:06:14.367 --> 00:06:17.667
Like, everything has tonality to it.

00:06:17.667 --> 00:06:20.868
-I wanted to test this tonight, if you don't mind.

00:06:20.868 --> 00:06:23.267
We have stuff here.

00:06:23.267 --> 00:06:26.200
Like, what could we do tonight?

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:27.901
-Well, what has sound to it?

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:29.868
Wait. Let me see that cup.

00:06:29.868 --> 00:06:31.200
-This cup? -Is there anything in it?

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.200
-Yeah, there's water. -Do you have anything I can tap?

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.968
-That has tea in it. That's for you. I have cups.

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:38.133
I have extra cups. Do you want a cup?

00:06:38.133 --> 00:06:39.701
-Wait. This is -- Yeah, give me a spoon

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:41.367
because I'm sure you have spoons somewhere.

00:06:41.367 --> 00:06:42.734
Take another "Tonight Show" cup.

00:06:42.734 --> 00:06:45.100
Yeah. I've marked up your table.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:49.067
So, okay. I hope this works. But every --

00:06:49.067 --> 00:06:52.300
[ Laughter ] Bear with me.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:53.767
Everything has tonality to it.

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:55.334
So if I were to --

00:06:55.334 --> 00:06:57.667
[ Rhythmic tapping ]

00:06:57.667 --> 00:06:59.267
[ Humming tone ]

00:06:59.267 --> 00:07:02.067
Here we go.

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:03.868
So that's kind of like a -- ♪ Ooh ♪

00:07:03.868 --> 00:07:06.400
If I had a way to record something,

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:10.033
I would, like, make a whole song out of this cup right now.

00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:13.067
-I have a way to record right now.

00:07:13.067 --> 00:07:14.467
-Wait.

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:18.200
[ Cheers and applause ] -No.

00:07:23.234 --> 00:07:24.601
[ Laughs ] -We got a setup.

00:07:24.601 --> 00:07:27.300
-No. -Oh, yeah, oh, yeah.

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:29.334
This is -- -Wait. Hold this.

00:07:29.334 --> 00:07:31.968
-I'll hold that.

00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:33.734
Charlie, we're always ready for you here at "The Tonight Show."

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:35.667
That's why we love when you come back.

00:07:35.667 --> 00:07:37.234
-Okay. -You're just making art.

00:07:37.234 --> 00:07:39.868
-What is this? This is Pro Tools, so...

00:07:39.868 --> 00:07:42.200
-I don't know how to do Pro Tools.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:45.934
-I thought your producer was joking when he said that he --

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:48.968
-If you even mention an idea, we're going to make it happen.

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:51.901
If it makes it on the air or not, we don't know, but...

00:07:51.901 --> 00:07:54.934
-Okay, so, everyone bear with us for a second.

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:57.634
I'm gonna -- Okay. So I'm gonna record --

00:07:57.634 --> 00:07:59.400
This is what I do on TikTok.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:02.334
I'm gonna do it on the show that started it all.

00:08:02.334 --> 00:08:04.968
You record a little -- [ Tapping ]

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:06.734
That's it. Wait. Hold on.

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.601
[ Tapping ] There. Ooh.

00:08:08.601 --> 00:08:09.767
[ Tapping ]

00:08:09.767 --> 00:08:11.868
I like the little -- Okay. Here. Take that.

00:08:11.868 --> 00:08:14.067
You can put that down. -You just got that.

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:15.634
-Okay. So... -♪ Dee-dee, dee-dee ♪

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:17.300
-Here it is. Can we get sound?

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:20.234
[ Tapping ] Ooh.

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:21.901
That's -- Here. Play that again.

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:25.067
This is -- There we go.

00:08:25.067 --> 00:08:27.367
So I can put it --

00:08:27.367 --> 00:08:28.801
[ Tapping ]

00:08:28.801 --> 00:08:30.367
There's the sound of the glass.

00:08:30.367 --> 00:08:32.367
But if you pitch it down...

00:08:32.367 --> 00:08:35.801
[ Tapping sound played as descending scale ]

00:08:35.801 --> 00:08:38.067
♪♪

00:08:38.067 --> 00:08:40.200
So that's just one note.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.501
I feel like I'm teaching all of a sudden.

00:08:42.501 --> 00:08:44.267
-This is like a master class! I love this.

00:08:44.267 --> 00:08:46.701
[ Vocalizing ]

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:52.100
♪♪

00:08:52.100 --> 00:08:54.033
So, this is what that sounds like here.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.367
[ Tapping echoing ]

00:08:55.367 --> 00:08:57.400
Ooh. We got reverb.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.567
Ugh.

00:08:58.567 --> 00:08:59.901
[ Tapping booms ]

00:08:59.901 --> 00:09:01.667
Too much. Wait.

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:03.701
So I can -- Okay. So, that's one layer.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:06.000
And I can add a little rhythm to it.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.100
Again, that's the cup sound.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:14.167
♪♪

00:09:14.167 --> 00:09:18.167
Okay. And then we need, like, a bass or something.

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:24.100
♪♪

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:26.234 --> 00:09:29.434
♪♪

00:09:29.434 --> 00:09:32.501
Oh, I'm not done.

00:09:32.501 --> 00:09:34.467
Okay, so that's looping.

00:09:34.467 --> 00:09:36.934
Again, these are all just cup sounds pitched down.

00:09:36.934 --> 00:09:39.133
If I put a kick drum, then you have a completed...

00:09:39.133 --> 00:09:40.968
[ Kick drum thumping ]

00:09:40.968 --> 00:09:43.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:45.133
♪♪

00:09:45.133 --> 00:09:47.467
-What?! -Wow.

00:09:47.467 --> 00:09:49.200
And there you go. That's a whole song.

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:52.100
-That's how you do it right there! Come on!

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:53.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:53.734 --> 00:09:57.701
Charlie Puth. That is amazing!

00:09:57.701 --> 00:09:59.901
"Charlie" is available right now,

00:09:59.901 --> 00:10:02.601
and he's performing for us later in the show.

00:10:02.601 --> 00:10:05.100
We'll be right back with Kate del Castillo.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.400
Stick around, everybody! -♪ Let's get it ♪

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:15.467
♪♪

